{"When provider does not return refresh token, code unconditionally sets hardcoded string 'refresh_token' instead of preserving previous real refresh token": 0.9715043902397156, "Minimal Zod schema uses computed property keys that collapse to single literal key and with default strip behavior drops fields like refresh_token from parsed response": 0.9072758555412292, "Token refresh logic assumes refreshOAuthTokens always returns object with .data property, but with credential sharing enabled it returns native fetch Response without .data, causing token to be undefined and access_token access to throw": 0.9834142327308655, "Using zod.parse throws on invalid request body resulting in unhandled exception and 500 response instead of clear 4xx error": 0.8979130387306213, "Webhook secret comparison uses potentially mixed-case environment variable name for header lookup, but Node.js normalizes header keys to lowercase, causing valid requests to be rejected with 403": 0.8369461297988892, "req.headers[...] can return a string[] when multiple header values are present, but the code compares it directly to a string without handling the array case": 0.5972514748573303, "Decryption call falls back to empty string when CALCOM_APP_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY env var is missing, causing symmetricDecrypt to throw with invalid key length and produce generic 500 error": 0.6285355091094971, "APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED constant is assigned result of logical AND between environment variables yielding string or undefined instead of boolean, breaking strict type expectations": 0.7678853869438171}